2026-09-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2259) 'how a session shapes its work
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2259) '- Branches start with a stage: `dev/`, `beta/`, `rc/`, `release/` or `archived/` (operator, 2026-10-12). A pushed branch is renamed through the code host's rename call, which keeps its pull request.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2259) '- After the stage, a name says what the work is: no `module-`, `godot-` or `vendor-` (operator, 2026-10-13).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2259) '- `dev/` becomes `beta/` once every latest check on the tip passed, the minimum bar (operator, 2026-10-13).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2259) '- A `dev/` branch ends as a pull request or in `archived/`; a fork keeps its `dev/`, `beta/`, `rc/` and `release/` branches (operator, 2026-10-17).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2259) '- Each RFD lands as one commit; a revision amends it before merge.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2259) '- Maintenance takes at most a tenth of a session's budget.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2259) '- RFD66606-2026 (commit messages), the subject line these commits use.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2259) '- RFD66606-2258, the gates each pushed branch runs.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Parked work
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Parked work is committed and pushed with its known defects named in the message, and the checkout is detached so `repo sync` cannot rebase it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Why the checkout is detached
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2259) '`repo sync` rebases a local branch that tracks the manifest's revision. A pushed branch loses nothing by being detached, and the next sync then leaves the project alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2259) 'When two names collide
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Dropping a prefix can land on a name that is already taken. Compare the two branches with `git cherry` both ways and `git diff --stat`. If one branch holds every patch of the other, keep it and delete the other; record the deleted tip in the report so it can be restored. If each holds work the other lacks, ask the operator: they may move the missing commits onto one branch and archive the other. A consumer that names branches, such as the assembly config, is updated in the same session, because the code host redirects a renamed branch's web links but not a `git fetch` of the old name.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2259) 'How a dev branch ends
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Sort each `dev/` branch by what it holds that the default branch lacks: `git cherry -v` against the default branch, and a trial merge with `git merge-tree --write-tree`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2259) '- Work the default branch lacks that merges cleanly goes to a pull request as it stands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2259) '- A branch whose commits the default branch mostly holds keeps only its `+` commits. They are cherry-picked onto a new `dev/<x>` off the default branch for a pull request, and the old branch is renamed to `archived/`, since a merge from a stale base conflicts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2259) '- Work in progress that was never built is renamed to `archived/`. A pull request would ask CI to judge code its author has not run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2259) 'A fork keeps every `dev/`, `beta/`, `rc/` and `release/` branch: its work still goes to a pull request, but the branch is neither renamed to `archived/` nor deleted when the pull request merges.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Before renaming, check that the `archived/` name is free and that no pull request has the branch as its head. After a pull request merges, cancel the merged branch's queued runs: they hold runners that the default branch's own run needs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2259) 'How a branch is promoted
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2259) 'Read the check runs of the branch tip with only the latest run of each check kept, so a superseded or cancelled run does not count against it. Promote only when nothing is queued or running, nothing failed, and the set of check names equals the default branch's. A run that passed on a base far behind the default branch passed against code that is no longer there, so the operator decides those case by case. A branch whose checks are still queued is promoted by a bounded watcher that re-reads the tip first and skips it if the tip moved.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2259  1 LINE
 Text:Written
